 black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]var-value-model[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]var-value-model: introduce the JSON value model (validation, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]normalization, caps) and the single canonical inline/block renderer in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase.core, widen agent_meta.json storage and readers to structured [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]values, and keep every existing consumer compiling and behaving [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]unchanged.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Full JSON output-variable values in the sase-core scan wire[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-wire-json[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-wire-json: generalize OutputVariableValue in the sase-core [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent-scan wire from text-or-string-list to a bounded JSON value, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]release sase-core, bump the sase-core-rs pin here, and widen the Python [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]wire marker type.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Authoring and consuming structured variables (CLI, Jinja, [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]STOP, skill, docs)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]var-cli-jinja[dim] · [dim][/dim]after var-value-model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]var-cli-jinja: add the `--json` value modifier and a `sase var list` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]display subcommand, pass containers into the Jinja `agents` namespace [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with JSON-shaped stringification, generalize STOP truthiness, and update[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the sase_var skill source and reference docs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]ACE renders structured variables in agent, clan, and tribe [/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD7